From: alioth iOS bring-up 2026-10-24
Subject: [PATCH] sweet: the K40's touch screen is FocalTech on GENI SE4, not Goodix on SE7 I2C

The previous driver described serial engine 7 as an I2C bus at 0xa84000
with a Goodix GT9896 at 0x5d. The Redmi K40 / POCO F3 has a FocalTech
part on serial engine 4 of qupv3_wrap0 (spi@990000), chip select on
gpio11, reset on gpio33, interrupt on gpio39, in 8640x19200 report space.
Its pin controller is at 0x0f000000 with the bus pins in the north tile
(0x0f900000) and reset/interrupt in the south (0x0f500000).

Ported from redwood_goodix.c (ios-alioth), whose PLATFORM_ALIOTH branch
was verified on this phone on 2026-10-22.

Verified here: real finger touches reach SpringBoard (v29, 2026-10-24).

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -1,9 +1,25 @@
 /*
- * SWEET SE7 FIFO I2C / GT9896 Yellowstone / Focaltech 54:52 bring-up.
- * Call once after the scheduler is running; all work runs on one thread.
- * Requires ABL-loaded GENI I2C firmware; votes L11C through sweet_rpmh.c.
- * No firmware/config upload or direct PMIC writes. Only IC data write:
- * zero to GT9896's event status after reading a report. See touch2/report.md.
+ * FocalTech touch screen on the Redmi K40 / POCO F3 (alioth, SM8250-AC).
+ *
+ * The chip sits on serial engine 4 of QUPV3 wrap 0 (spi@990000), chip select is
+ * its own pin (gpio11), reset is gpio33 and the interrupt line is gpio39. It
+ * keeps its firmware in its own flash and starts it as soon as reset is
+ * released, so no firmware download is involved. There is only one touch part
+ * on this phone: no Goodix variant, no ID straps to read.
+ *
+ * Ported from redwood_goodix.c (ios-alioth), whose PLATFORM_ALIOTH branch was
+ * verified on this same phone on 2026-10-22 (real finger touches reaching
+ * SpringBoard). The earlier version of this file described serial engine 7 as
+ * an I2C bus at 0xa84000 with a Goodix GT9896 at 0x5d, which is not this board.
+ *
+ * There is no clock, pin, regulator or SPI framework in this kernel, so this
+ * driver does all of it itself, in the vendor driver's order: power (two RPMh
+ * regulators), clocks (GCC votes and the engine's RCG), pins (three TLMM
+ * tiles), then the engine in FIFO mode. If the engine cannot be used the same
+ * four pins are driven by hand.
+ *
+ * Touches are handed to SweetHID (iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp) as panel
+ * pixels; the chip reports in 8640 x 19200 and the panel is 1080 x 2400.
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 #include <sys/param.h>
