+/*
+ * kona's pin controller is one 16 MB block at 0x0f000000 whose tiles are not
+ * evenly spaced (pinctrl-kona.c): north is +0x00900000, south is +0x00500000,
+ * and a pin's registers are at tile + 0x1000 * pin. The bus pins (8, 9, 10,
+ * 11) are in the north tile; reset (33) and interrupt (39) are in the south.
+ * Reading a pin through the wrong base returns 0, which is what a pin whose
+ * registers are never touched looks like.
